# What a source archive should not carry.
#
# GitHub's own ZIPs ("Download ZIP", and the one behind every tag) are
# git archives, so this list decides what a stranger downloads. The test
# suite is the reason it matters: it holds real attack strings as
# fixtures, because its job is to prove the connector refuses them. A
# server-side firewall such as ModSecurity reads the upload, sees
# "document.cookie" and "<script>alert(1)</script>" and refuses the
# whole plugin at the WordPress upload screen.
/tests          export-ignore
/.github        export-ignore
/.gitattributes export-ignore
/.gitignore     export-ignore
/composer.json  export-ignore
/composer.lock  export-ignore
